# The free fast path's route byte: each wrapper is one core atomic
# operation (or AtomicU8::new), and `fixed` is kept because fetch_or of
# bits within ROUTE is the only write after `new`.
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): the byte's AtomicU8 is private to this
# file, and each wrapper is called once, in heap/shared.rs, with the one
# raw write through `S_FREE_FLAGS` writing the byte `new` made
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). Every write after `new` is a `fetch_or`
# within ROUTE, so every value in the byte's modification order keeps the
# made bits, and C++20's coherence rules ([intro.races]) give a reader
# ordered after `init` one of those values, for any ordering. The flags
# models check that on copies of the `Shared` steps
# (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The GenMC flags cases run the same wrappers'
# bodies over `core`'s atomic, inside pinned copies of the same steps
# (tests/genmc/flags.rs, `GENMC_PINS`), with the permissions erased
# (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC").
new	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::flags_route_byte, and loom: flags::loom_flags_route_byte_keeps_push_flags and flags::loom_flags_two_builders, and GenMC: flags1 [rc11 imm] and flags2 [rc11 imm arm8]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Shared` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/flags.rs states, and beyond the configurations tests/genmc/flags.rs states, which the GenMC cases run it in as it is over `core`'s atomic inside copies of the same steps, each only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); that `fixed` is kept when the byte is moved into place (`put_flags`' `ptr::write`); the wrapper's contract under weak memory, which no GenMC case checks (the cases erase the permissions, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so none sees a ghost value); that no write but these reaches the byte, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 2266153701, body 4057886722
